SCENE STRUCTURE

P0 — Dynamic Anchor (0.0–0.3s)
Ultra-macro on intertwined fibers vibrating with micro-airflow.
Camera pulls back in a rapid but smooth dolly-out revealing the scale of the woven wave.
Fibers tremble like a storm about to break.

P1 — Approach (0.3–2.0s)

Side-tracking shot, 35mm lens.
The girl pedals forward, wind tearing her hair.
Behind her, the thread-wave begins rising violently, threads peeling upward like storm banners.
Camera drifts in and out of shallow DOF, parallaxing her against the giant mass.

P2 — Wave Rising (2.0–4.0s)

Low-angle hero shot, ultra-wide 14mm.
The wave curls overhead, millions of intertwined yarns forming a colossal crest.
Loose fragments tear off and spiral toward the lens.
Camera arcs upward and backward in a rising swoop.

P3 — Wheel Spin Macro (4.0–6.0s)

Macro orbit around the bike wheels.
Threads get caught between spokes, glowing with friction as they whip outward.
Camera rotates 270° around the wheel, then whip-pans up toward the wave.

P4 — Vertical Turbulence (6.0–9.0s)

Camera rockets upward above the girl.
Looking down, we see the wave collapsing in slow-motion turbulence—layered, fractal thread structures folding over themselves.
Fiber-clouds burst upward like debris from an explosion.
Lens shake on major impacts.

P5 — Into the Surge (9.0–13.5s)

Front-facing tracking shot, 18mm lens.
The girl pedals directly toward the viewer, illuminated by swirling pastel fiber-wind.
The collapsing wave behind her unleashes a tidal roll of yarn-mist that envelops her.
Threads whip past camera in high-speed streaks.
Massive parallax to emphasize speed.

